course: dictionary
lesson: 6623
title: Notch: a cut, a step, a score
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A notch is a small V-shaped cut in an edge or surface. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump, and even with its eyes shut it can see through notches in its eyelids.» The sentence is about eyelids, so a notch must be a small cut or gap, not a big hole.
explain: «Tiger sharks eat almost anything, from fish, turtles, sea snakes and birds to rubbish like tyres and number plates, reported; their notched teeth cut turtle shells.» The word notched tells you the teeth have small V-shaped cuts in their edges, which help them cut through shells.
explain: Notch also means a step on a scale: turn the heat up a notch means turn it up one step. Notch up is informal and means to score or achieve something, as in notch up a win. Top-notch means excellent. Check each meaning by putting it into the sentence and asking whether it still makes sense.
fact: A notch is a small V-shaped cut in an edge or surface.
fact: «Notch» can mean one level or step on a scale, as in «turn the volume up a notch».
fact: «Notched» means having small V-shaped cuts in it, like the «notched teeth» of some tiger sharks.
fact: «Notch up» means to achieve or score, as in «notch up a win».
fact: «Top-notch» means excellent, the very best.
exercise: «Even with its eyes shut, the potoo can see through notches in its eyelids.» What is a notch? | A large bird that sleeps all day | A type of cloud | A loud sound made by a bird | *A small V-shaped cut in an edge or surface
exercise: «Turn the heat up a notch.» What does a notch mean here? | *One step up on a scale | A spoon made of metal | A bird's nest | A small cut in a piece of wood
exercise: Ella says, «The team managed to notch up a win.» What does notch up mean? | To cut a hole in the field | To lose a game badly | To sleep through the match | *To score or achieve a win
test: «Their notched teeth cut turtle shells.» What does notched describe? | A soft, slippery tail | A long fin | Sea snakes that are very quiet | *Teeth with small V-shaped cuts in them
test: Sam says, «That chef's cooking is top-notch.» What does top-notch mean? | *Excellent, the very best | Burnt and cold | Very tall and thin | Slow to serve
exam: Read this: «The potoo's eyelids have notches, and the tiger shark has notched teeth.» Which word means a small V-shaped cut? | shark | eyelid | *notch | potoo
